Antonio,

As mentioned in the original query, I am testing on a single node Hadoop cluster and all the dependencies were installed. But, I installed the dependecies for rmr2/rhdfs in a custom directory (~/R/x86_64-pc-linux-gnu-library/3.0) instead of the system directory. As suggested, I ran R as sudo and then installed the dependencies in the system path and everything works fine.

Thanks for the hint. I was struggling to get around the problem. Not sure why the dependencies need to be included in the system folder, may be this can be added in the installations instructions to help others.

Thanks,
Praveen

